      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to North Carolina?",
      "a": "North Carolina has $4.2B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. The state recorded $6.7B in FY21, $8.6B in FY22, $7B in FY23, $7.2B in FY24, and $9.3B in FY25, showing the FY26 total is lower than recent years. The state has 153,408 awards this fiscal year and an average award size of $27.2K."
